{"id":"33729f44de662a101da37dda9a47857bd5c477ab","axis":"silent","repo":"Azure/azure-sdk-for-js","sha":"33729f44de662a101da37dda9a47857bd5c477ab","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"sdk/monitor/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -9,12 +9,14 @@"," "," ### Bugs Fixed"," ","+- Closed exporter-owned connections after each temporary overflow routing request, while preserving connection reuse for cached routes and caller-owned transports. [#40586](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/pull/40586)"," - Preserved compatible sampler attribute value types for OpenTelemetry 2.x consumers while including the numeric sample-rate attribute in the return type. [#40536](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/pull/40536)"," "," ## 1.0.0-beta.47 (2026-11-05)"," "," ### Features Added"," ","+- Added opt-in multi-endpoint routing for logs, traces, and metrics, with a 64-route cache and sequential temporary senders for overflow destinations. [#40586](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/pull/40586)"," - Added automatic gzip request compression for Azure Monitor ingestion, including internal Statsbeat and customer SDK Stats, while preserving uncompressed requests to custom ingestion domains and falling back to the original request if compression fails. [#40414](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/pull/40414)"," - Added an opt-in 4 MiB limit for `gen_ai.input.messages` and `gen_ai.output.messages` through `APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=gen_ai_input_output_limit_increase`. Default GenAI limits remain at 256 KiB, and all other custom dimensions remain limited to 8 KiB. [#40609](https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-js/pull/40609)"," "],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdk/monitor/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter/README.md","lines":["@@ -155,6 +155,56 @@ Availability records use the same correlation context as other OpenTelemetry log"," "," If any required attribute is missing or empty, the exporter sends the record as regular message telemetry instead. Exception and custom event attributes take precedence over availability attributes."," ","+### Multi-endpoint routing (preview)","+","+Set `APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES=multi_endpoint_routing` before constructing","+any exporter to route logs, spans, and metric data points to different Application Insights","+resources. Routing is disabled by default. A host connection string is optional.","+","+Each item must supply `microsoft.instrumentation_key` and `microsoft.ingestion_endpoint`","+as attributes. The endpoint must be an absolute HTTPS URL without credentials, query strings,","+or fragments. Items with missing or invalid destinations are dropped, not sent to the host.","+**Use trusted, server-owned destination configuration, not request headers or baggage.**","+","+```ts snippet:ReadmeSampleMultiEndpointRouting","+import { LoggerProvider, BatchLogRecordProcessor } from \"@opentelemetry/sdk-logs\";","+import { AzureMonitorLogExporter } from \"@azure/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter\";","+","+process.env.APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_EXPERIMENTAL_FEATURES = \"multi_endpoint_routing\";","+","+const provider = new LoggerProvider({","+  processors: [","+    new BatchLogRecordProcessor({","+      exporter: new AzureMonitorLogExporter(),","+    }),","+  ],","+});","+","+provider.getLogger(\"routed-logs\").emit({","+  body: \"Order completed\",","+  attributes: {","+    \"microsoft.instrumentation_key\": \"<destination instrumentation key>\",","+    \"microsoft.ingestion_endpoint\": \"https://<region>.in.applicationinsights.azure.com\",","+    \"microsoft.multi_endpoint_cloud_role\": \"orders\",","+  },","+});","+```","+","+Set the same attributes on spans or individual metric data points to route those signals.","+Span events inherit their parent span's routing attributes. Resource and instrumentation-scope","+attributes are not used for metric routing.","+","+For Microsoft Entra ID authentication, set `microsoft.ingestion_auth` to `\"aad\"` and","+provide an exporter `credential`. Otherwise, items use key-only authentication, even if","+a credential is configured. AAD routes without a credential fail.","+","+Set `microsoft.multi_endpoint_cloud_role` to specify the cloud role name. It defaults to","+`unknown_service`. Role instances still come from the resource.","+","+Offline retry storage supports up to 64 endpoint/authentication pairs per exporter.","+Custom `httpClient` and `retryOptions` are supported, but `pipeline` and `additionalPolicies`","+are not supported in routing mode.","+"," ### Sampling"," "," You can enable sampling to limit the amount of telemetry records you receive. In order to enable correct sampling in Application Insights, use the `ApplicationInsightsSampler` as shown below."],"additions":50,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdk/monitor/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter/review/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter-node.api.md","lines":["@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ export abstract class AzureMonitorBaseExporter {","     // @internal","     protected readonly _increaseGenAiMessageLimit: boolean;","     protected instrumentationKey: string;","+    protected readonly multiEndpointRouting: boolean;","     protected trackStatsbeat: boolean;"," }"," "],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"sdk/monitor/monitor-opentelemetry-exporter/src/config.ts","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ export interface ApplicationInsightsClientOptionalParams"," export interface AzureMonitorExporterOptions extends ApplicationInsightsClientOptionalParams {","   /**","    * Azure Monitor Connection String, if not provided the exporter will try to use environment variable APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING","+   * Optional when the multi_endpoint_routing experimental feature is enabled.","    * Ex: \"InstrumentationKey=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000;IngestionEndpoint=https://dc.services.visualstudio.com\"","    */","   connectionString?: string;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":